# FINAL DEVELOPMENT INSTRUCTIONS

Before writing code:

1. Review the entire project structure.
2. Identify the existing framework and integrations.
3. Assess whether the architecture can support multi-user, multi-branch operations.
4. Identify missing functionality.
5. Create a detailed implementation plan.
6. Establish the database schema.
7. Define the core user journeys.
8. Define the security architecture.

Then implement the application phase by phase.

Do not unnecessarily replace working functionality.

Do not create fake dashboards populated with hardcoded numbers.

Do not use mock data as a substitute for working features.

Do not create buttons that do nothing.

Do not claim payment integration is complete without successful end-to-end testing.

Do not claim barcode scanning works without testing it on actual supported devices.

Do not compromise security for development convenience.

Every major feature must connect to the real database and backend.

Use realistic sample data only in a clearly separated demonstration environment.

Keep the interface consistent throughout the application.

The application should be built for real businesses, real employees, real transactions and real financial accountability.

